00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:30,180
Just go ahead and search for 'Cursor' yourself. Configuring a proxy should get you all set.

186
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:31,480
So, what's the third step?

187
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:32,780
So, before we start writing any code...

188
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:35,220
First, you absolutely need to understand Cursor's four working modes.

189
00:06:35,220 --> 00:06:35,820
This is super important.

190
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:37,990
In the bottom-left corner of the chat box, there's a dropdown menu.

191
00:06:37,990 --> 00:06:39,210
And there are four options in here.

192
00:06:39,210 --> 00:06:40,570
The first one is Agent mode.

193
00:06:40,570 --> 00:06:42,070
This is the most comprehensive mode.

194
00:06:42,070 --> 00:06:44,890
And it's also the mode most commonly used by our non-technical folks.

195
00:06:44,890 --> 00:06:46,330
You just tell it what you need.

196
00:06:46,330 --> 00:06:47,870
It doesn't just give you the answers,

197
00:06:47,870 --> 00:06:50,110
It will also actually get to work and write the code for you.

198
00:06:50,110 --> 00:06:50,930
creating files,

199
00:06:50,930 --> 00:06:51,850
modify files,

200
00:06:51,850 --> 00:06:53,800
to build this project from the ground up.

201
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:56,140
The second one is the Plan Mode.

202
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:59,160
So this mode basically takes the planning capability and breaks it out as a separate function.

203
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:00,790
It's all talk and no action.

204
00:07:00,790 --> 00:07:03,270
It will lay out a very detailed plan for you to make changes.

205
00:07:03,270 --> 00:07:05,190
It tells you which file to modify in the first step,

206
00:07:05,190 --> 00:07:06,840
what logic to add in the second step,

207
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:08,820
Once you've confirmed that the plan looks good,

208
00:07:08,820 --> 00:07:10,900
Then you switch to Agent mode to execute it.

209
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:12,620
So, what about when you're dealing with complex logic?

210
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:14,200
First, let's use 'plan', and we can take a look.

211
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:16,830
This way, you can prevent the AI from messing up your code.

212
00:07:16,830 --> 00:07:18,730
The third one is Debug mode.

213
00:07:18,730 --> 00:07:19,750
And this one, as the name suggests...

214
00:07:19,750 --> 00:07:21,280
It's specifically for fixing bugs.

215
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:22,780
You just feed it the error log,

216
00:07:22,780 --> 00:07:25,440
It will analyze the cause by looking at the code across your entire project.

217
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:27,590
and gives you the fix directly.

218
00:07:27,590 --> 00:07:30,070
The fourth option is the Ask mode.

219
00:07:30,070 --> 00:07:32,540
It's basically a pure Q&A mode.

220
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:33,600
It only reads, it doesn't write.

221
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:34,980
It won't touch your code.

222
00:07:34,980 --> 00:07:36,180
If you come across a concept you don't understand,

223
00:07:36,180 --> 00:07:38,460
or if you want the AI to explain the logic of a piece of code.

224
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:39,940
So just use it, it's super convenient.

225
00:07:39,940 --> 00:07:41,420
So, speaking of these four modes,

226
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:44,600
Now, a lot of people who are new to Cursor tend to get them mixed up pretty easily.

227
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,280
So, when you're frequently using the 'Plan' mode,

228
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:47,680
and just jump straight into Agent mode,

229
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:48,880
And what happens? The AI just goes on a wild spree of changes.

